  "details": "When I'm taking a selfie with a friend, if THEY are the one holding the camera, I can only guess whether I'm in frame, whether my hands are positioned right, etc.  It would be nice to have the option for a friend's camera to actually show its viewfinder (aka its screen), rather than just the little circle.  (Maybe it would be something that you activate by clicking their camera once they equip it, so you don't have to worry about performance being impacted in situations where you DON'T care what their camera is doing.  If even THAT situation causes performance conerns, maybe it could even be enforced that this feature can't be enabled while your camera is also out -- that way, the performance is no different than having your own camera out would have been.)",
